  But again, lojban doesn't necessarily divide up the world in the same way
as any other given schema/language does, for good or ill.  Since you
specifically want to ask about the periodic table, we can questions like,
"why isn't there a gismu for the lanthanides, or the actinides, haolgens,
or heck, even 'radioactive'?" jinme includes alloys, etc. We have a word,
ratni, that can used to specify elemental compunds.  But again, we're
talking about a language that (at least on a gismu level) differentiates
between rats and mice, but doesn't even have a word for "rodent".  That
classes worms and mollusks together, lumps tigers and cheetahs and panthers
(but not lions get their won), etc.

               --geyspa

